# Migrations are tracked. This used to be an ignore-by-default rule with one
# `!` exception per file, which meant every new migration needed a matching
# line and forgetting one dropped it from the commit silently — `git add -A`
# reports nothing, and the omission only surfaces on deploy as a missing
# table. Ignore the scratch output of `alembic revision --autogenerate`
# instead, which is the file that should not be committed unedited.
alembic/versions/*_autogen_*.py
node_modules/
